-- title:
--   A small answer is an exact exponent bracket.
-- statement:
--   A small answer is an exact exponent bracket. Saturation means the largest prescribed
--   power was actually reached. No comparison against that potentially enormous power is
--   performed on the branch that stops early.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.fieldProxy_word_length`, `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.framed_raw_halt`, `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.logProxyProgram_bounded_run`.
